<title>USA: EU's Brittan defends EMU criteria interpretation.</title>
<headline>EU's Brittan defends EMU criteria interpretation.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union Trade Commissioner Leon Brittan said vaguely-worded convergence criteria for a proposed single European currency will not be used to facilitate marginal nations entry.</p>
<p>&quot;They will not be used as an opportunity to depart from the central objective and the reason for that is the adherence to those criteria will determine whether the project is successful and gets off to a good start,&quot; said Brittan in an interview with Reuters Financial Television.  </p>
<p>&quot;These convergence criteria will be interpreted in good faith,&quot; Brittan said.</p>
<p>&quot;Where they are precise they will be interpreted precisely. Where they talk about looking to see the degree of progress in a direction, that is exactly what will be looked at in good faith,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
